27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #A few observations, roughly in order of impact:
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #**Dropped sends during connect/reconnect.** `send` silently discards messages whenever `readyState` isn't OPEN. Since the module's loop starts immediately after construction, the first several ticks are almost certainly lost before the handshake completes, and every reconnect window loses more. Options: buffer outgoing messages and flush them in `onOpen`, or have `send` return success/failure so the loop can react.
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #**Unguarded `JSON.parse`.** A malformed (or binary) frame will throw inside `onMessage`. Wrapping in try/catch and ignoring or logging bad frames would keep the connection stable. Related: if the Godot side ever sends binary, `event.data` arrives as a Blob and parse fails.
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #**Echo feedback risk.** Every inbound message triggers an outbound `echo`. If the server acknowledges or responds to the echo request, you get a loop. Fine if the server ignores unknown methods, but worth being deliberate about.
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #**No teardown.** After the loop finishes, the client continues reconnecting forever. Also, under HMR (Vite etc.), a module re-run creates a second client while the old one is still reconnecting. A `stop`/`close` method that nulls the handlers and clears the reconnect timer would fix both.
27a4bcc0 [glm-5.3] #
