27a4bcc1 [glm-5.3] #- Ids are assigned but responses are never correlated; if you later want request/response semantics, a pending-id map would slot in naturally.
27a4bcc1 [glm-5.3] #- If `strictPropertyInitialization` is on, `ws` needs a definite assignment assertion since TS can't see that `connect` assigns it.
27a4bcc1 [glm-5.3] #- Class naming convention is PascalCase (`StartgClient`), and `sendCount` reads more like `nextId`.
27a4bcc1 [glm-5.3] #
27a4bcc1 [glm-5.3] #The overall shape is a sensible dev harness — the reconnect-on-close pattern and handler binding are fine. Happy to sketch the buffered-send or teardown changes if you'd like.
