280d7bc6 [deepseek-flash] #Actually the existing code has a built-in verification in `base64()`, so if it were broken they'd see it. So the encoder probably works for most inputs but the `,`/`/` asymmetry at index 63 is a real edge case.
280d7bc6 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc6 [deepseek-flash] #Hmm, wait. Let me reconsider. `(b0<<shift)>>2` - for shift=6: `(b0<<6)>>2` = b0<<4. If b0 = 0xFF, that's 0xFF0, &0x3f = 0x30 = 48. And `b1>>(10-6)` = b1>>4. So sixbits = (0x30 | (b1>>4)) & 0x3f. Bits: 0x30 has bits 4,5 set. b1>>4 gives bits 0-3 = high nibble of b1. So combined: bits 0-3 from b1 high nibble, bits 4-5 from b0 bits 0-1 (since b0<<4 puts b0 bit0 at bit4, bit1 at bit5). Yes that's correct for shift=6 (6 bits: 2 from b0, 4 from b1).
280d7bc6 [deepseek-flash] #
