280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #Let me write it.
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #=================
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #Thanks for sharing the whole `native/` tree. A few observations, grouped roughly by how much they
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #matter. I've stuck to things that look like real defects or genuine design decisions rather than
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #style preferences.
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #Cross‑cutting patterns
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #• Header‑only functions without `inline`/`static`.* Many headers define free functions at
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #namespace scope (`strip`, `base64`, `safeString`, `loadString`, `elapsedNanos`, `markUp`,
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #`int8`/`int16`/`int32`, the whole `openPort`/`listPorts` block, `testVideo`, etc.). Any TU that
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #includes two of these — or includes one from two TUs — will get duplicate symbol errors or ODR
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #violations. `select.h` is the worst case: it has no include guard at all and defines `main()`.
280d7bc7 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #• Globals in headers. `previousNanos` (clocks.h), `infoCache[1024]` (bluetooth.h),
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #`frame_data/frame_size/frame_type/frame_number` and `struct v4l2_buffer buf` (video.h),
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #`emptyString` (udev.h), `Stereo stereo` (headless.h), `const char *path = "/dev/null"`
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #(headless.h) are all non‑`static`, non‑`inline`. Same duplicate‑symbol problem, plus the usual
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #name‑collision risk from `path`, `buf`, `fd`, `io`, `buffers`, `dev_name`.
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #• Signed/unsigned conversions.* This is the one I'd fix first because it can corrupt
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #memory, not just misreport:
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #- `Process::readBytes` returns `size_t` but the underlying `read()` returns `ssize_t`. A `-1`
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #becomes `SIZE_MAX`, and `Device::runRead` only breaks on `n == 0`, then does `onRead({buffer,
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #buffer + n})`. That's an out‑of‑bounds read.
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #- Same shape in `SocketConnection::readBytes` returning `(size_t)result` from a `int`.
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #- `HttpConnection::onRequest`: `size_t start = ss.tellg();` then `n -= start;` — `tellg()` returns
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #`-1` on failure, and the subsequent `recv` length arithmetic mixes the two domains.
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #File‑specific
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #• nitrohost.h* — `loadString` leaks an fd on every call. The loop returns from inside
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #(`return 2` / `return 0`), so `close(fd)` is unreachable. On a long‑running server (`fit3.cpp`)
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #that adds up fast.
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc8 [deepseek-flash] #• bitmap.h* — `setColor` calls `rgb888(r, b, g)` for the 4‑byte case while `rgb888` is
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #`(r<<16)|(g<<8)|b`. Green and blue are swapped for 32‑bit surfaces. The 16‑bit path looks correct.
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #• synth.h — `AudioBuffer::area` uses `double total;` uninitialised before accumulation.
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #Also the `#else` branch of `mixPCM` still takes `snd_pcm_t pcm`, but `snd_pcm_t` is only
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #declared when `USE_ALSA_AUDIO` is defined, so that branch won't compile in a non‑ALSA build.
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #• json.h* — the control‑character scan is `if (c < 9)`. That misses `\t` through `\x1f`;
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #the JSON spec disallows all of them unescaped. Should be `< 0x20`. Separately, the parser is built
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #on `std::wstring_convert`/`codecvt_utf8<wchar_t>`, which is deprecated in C++17 and removed in
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #C++26 — worth planning a replacement.
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #• redis.h* — `replyGraph` uses `r->str` for `REDIS_REPLY_INTEGER`; `str` is NULL for
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #integers, so this is undefined behaviour on any integer reply. Also `RedisContext::graph` doesn't
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #take `contextMutex` while `run` does — the locking discipline is inconsistent.
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #• base64.h* — the encode and decode alphabets differ at index 63 (`Encode64` has `,`,
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #`Decode64` has `/`). Any byte pattern that maps to 63 will round‑trip through `base64()` and fail
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #the built‑in verification. Worth either reconciling the tables or documenting that encoding is
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #deliberately non‑standard.
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bc9 [deepseek-flash] #• crypto.h* — the name says SHA‑512 but `evpSHA512HashBytes` calls `EVP_sha3_512()`. If
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #that's intentional, the function names are misleading; if not, it's a silent algorithm change. Also
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #the `CommonCrypto` path ignores `salt` entirely while the OpenSSL path mixes it in — the two
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #backends produce different hashes for the same input, which will bite any persisted credentials.
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #• connections.h — `udev udev;` is used before initialisation:
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #`udev_enumerate_new(udev)` is called with an uninitialised pointer. Should be `udev_new()`.
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #• eglgraphics.h* — `createBuffer(GLenum, GLint buffer)` takes `buffer` by value, so the
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #generated GL handle never reaches the caller. In `init`, the `glBindBuffer` call is commented out,
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #so the subsequent `glVertexAttribPointer` binds nothing.
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #• video.h* — `testVideo` calls `init_device()` before `open_device()`, and `init_device`
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #does all its ioctls on `fd` (still `-1`). Order should be swapped.
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #• headless.h* — `Process::start` uses `vfork()` in what is clearly a multi‑threaded server
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #(threads are created elsewhere in the same process). `vfork` in a multithreaded process is
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #undefined behaviour; `fork()` is the safe choice, and the comment about "works weel from fork"
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #suggests this has already been noticed. Also `makeargv` uses file‑scope `static` buffers and is not
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #reentrant.
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #• drmdisplay.h* — `setMode` reads the CRTC but never calls `drmModeSetCrtc`; the mode is
280d7bca [deepseek-flash] #only applied on the first `flip()`. That may be deliberate, but the function name oversells what it
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #does. The commented‑out `drmModeFreeCrtc(crtcId)` wouldn't have compiled anyway (`crtcId` is an
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #`int`).
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #• fit3.cpp* — `signalHandler` calls `std::this_thread::sleep_for`, `closeHttpTasks`,
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #`std::cout` and `exit`. None of those are async‑signal‑safe. `exit` in particular can deadlock if
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #the signal arrives while a stream lock is held.
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #• xml.h* — `xmlCleanupParser()` is called after every document. The libxml2 docs
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #specifically say it should be called once at program exit; calling it repeatedly in a long‑running
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #process is not supported.
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #• opensocket.h / .cpp* — `SocketConnection::onRead` is a no‑op, so anything received on a
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #socket device is discarded before it reaches the buffer. If that's not intentional, `runRead` is
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #doing work for nothing. Also `Socket::listen`/`accept` are Windows‑only stubs on POSIX, which is a
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #surprising asymmetry for a cross‑platform class.
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #• select.h* — no include guard, defines `main()`, and looks like a copy‑pasted tutorial
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #snippet rather than something intended to be included. Probably wants to be a `.cpp` or removed.
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #Things that look good
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcb [deepseek-flash] #- The `HexImage` IHEX parser is careful about checksum, record type, and the `:00000001FF`
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #terminator, and correctly handles the `DT_DIR`/`DT_REG` cases in `scanFSFolder`.
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #- `escape()` in nitrohost.h does the full JSON control‑character range correctly (including
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #`\uXXXX`), which makes the inconsistency in `parseJSON`'s scanner more noticeable.
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #- The OSC reader in `opensocket.cpp` correctly 4‑byte aligns address and format strings and handles
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #network byte order for floats.
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #- The `Redis`/`Sink`/`Scribe` split is a clean way to separate blocking command use from streaming
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #consumption.
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #- `readWav` handles the `subchunkSize > 16` skip properly, which a lot of small WAV readers get
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #wrong.
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #If you want, I can go deeper on any one of these — the two I'd prioritise are the
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #`size_t`/`ssize_t` conversions in the device layer (memory safety) and the `loadString` fd leak
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #(will exhaust descriptors under the `fit3` server load).
280d7bcc [deepseek-flash] #
